  "comment": "A real same-asset (1:1) multichain wallet_prepareCalls from relay-staging, captured 2026-10-15 (celo-harness/evidence/2026-10-15-spine-local-11-31-31-wire.json, entry 33): a first-time registry write on Ethereum Sepolia (0xaa36a7) funded from Celo Sepolia (0xaa044c). quotes[0] is the source leg (escrow on Celo, fee in CELO), quotes[1] the destination leg (fee in ETH, encodedFundTransfers pulled from the relay funder). Both legs are charged in their chain's native token and the relay's testnet config makes 1 CELO repay 1 ETH, which is what the SDK's old single-number fee read depended on. The wallet's outgoing CELO asset diff is the escrow it locks, not the leg's fee.",
